WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:01.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's wonderful
to have you back.

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's good to be back.
I love you.

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love this show.
I love your stories.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:07.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
And you are loved, as well.

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:09.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
You are also -- You've been
doing this a long time.

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:10.677 line:92%
You're very recognizable.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:11.578 line:92%
When you're back in New York,

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:13.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
are you recognized
on the street?

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:13.747 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-You talk about love.

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:16.750
You know, I am in New York,
and I'm here -- Well, obviously.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I'm here promoting, you know,

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:20.420 line:92%
"Deal or No Deal" on CNBC.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.689
But when I'm in New York,
as opposed to where I live

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:25.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
in Los Angeles,
you are much more exposed...

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:26.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-...to people.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:28.795 size:81% position:41%
You know, you show up
at a backdoor in L.A.,

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:30.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you go in,
and you don't see people.

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
But here, you know,
walking across the street

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:34.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
from "The Today Show"
or here or in the lobby,

00:00:34.401 --> 00:00:35.268 size:81% position:41% line:92%
there's people around.

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:38.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I've learned
a 10-second rule.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:40.673 size:84% position:42%
And the 10-second rule
that I have learned is,

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:43.810
once somebody approaches you,
and they're very nice to you

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:44.911 line:92%
and they give you a compliment,

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:47.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
you better leave
within 10 seconds,

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:49.682 size:81% position:41% line:92%
because it turns ugly.

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:52.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
Somebody will come up to me
and say,

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:55.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I saw you promoting
'Deal or No Deal' on CNBC.

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:57.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love that show!"
And I go, "Thank you."

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:01.995
"It's so much better than 'AGT.'
You are not good on that show."

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:03.763 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:06.266
You know? Or, "I saw you
last night on television.

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:07.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were so funny."
"Thank you."

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:11.337
"And in person, you are fatter."
You know?

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:11.871 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.871 --> 00:01:14.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just never --
And people in New York

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.408 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
are so, like --

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:16.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
This happened the last time
I was here,

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:19.012
and I ended up talking about it
in my act, but it's real,

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:20.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it happened
when I was doing your show.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:23.149
I met somebody downstairs,
and they go, "Howie Mandel!"

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I go, "Yes."
And they go, "I love you.

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:27.487
From the time I was a kid,
I watched 'Bobby's World,'

00:01:27.487 --> 00:01:30.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
I watched 'St. Elsewhere,'
we watch 'AGT.'

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:33.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
We watch everything you do.
I just love you."

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:36.930
And I said,
"Well, what are you doing now?"

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:37.630 line:92%
They go, "We're tourists.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.732
We're just hanging around,
but we're from New York."

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:41.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I go,
"Well, I'm going upstairs.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:44.671 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I'm doing 'Seth Meyers.'

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:46.973
You could probably come with me.
You want to come up?"

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:49.142 line:92%
And they just said, "Nah."

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:51.644 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:52.145 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Nah."

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:55.915
-Howie, I feel liking that story
reflects badly on me.

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.050 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, they love everything
you've been in,

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:01.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the first time
they said no

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:02.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
was when you tried to get them
to see me.

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:03.656 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Think about this --

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:05.925
You have been talking to me
for more than 10 seconds.

00:02:05.925 --> 00:02:07.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's true.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:09.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
I made the mistake.
I made the mistake.

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:12.799
I want to ask you about this.
You've been very open about --

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:15.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were a germophobe.
-Were? I am.

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:16.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You am. You are.
Yes.

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:19.005
-It's very hard for me.
I'm always around people.

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:19.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I fly.

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:22.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that's the thing.
I feel, you know, obviously,

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:23.843 size:75% position:38%
I know now we're not
gonna shake hands.

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:24.577 size:84% position:42% line:92%
We're gonna bump fists.

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:26.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you get on a plane --
a plane is a plane.

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:28.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
It doesn't care.
-You're right.

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:30.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
Things happen to me that don't
happen to other people.

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:33.653
I think when you have that --
You bring it upon yourself.

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:37.323
I'm so -- I'll tell you, this is
not a touching or a germ thing.

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:40.226 line:92%
But I was on a plane recently,

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:43.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the guy next to me
took off his shoes.

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:44.297 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience groans ]

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:46.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were you in there?
Did you smell it?

00:02:46.332 --> 00:02:46.866 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:50.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was an odor,
the worst odor I have ever --

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:52.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you can't say to the guy,
you know --

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:54.440
So I went up front, and I spoke
to the flight attendant.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:57.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "The guy beside me
took off his shoes,

00:02:57.343 --> 00:03:01.214 size:84% position:42%
and I can't breathe,
and it's just horrible.

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:03.783 line:92%
Is there any way -- you as --"

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:05.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
She says,
"I'll take care of it."

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:06.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
So she went.
I stayed you up there.

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
She went.
And I saw her talking,

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:10.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then I see the guy
roll his eyes,

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:13.293
and he takes his shoes,
and he puts them back on.

00:03:13.293 --> 00:03:14.394 line:92%
And I go back to the seat.

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:16.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is the weirdest thing
in the world.

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:19.065 line:92%
It turns out it wasn't his feet.

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:21.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
His ankles stink.
-Oh!

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:26.206
So even when the shoes went back
on, the smell was still there.

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:27.807 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Both laugh ]

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:29.275 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-How does that happen?

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:30.777 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:33.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
And how do you know
it's his ankles?

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:34.113 line:92%
This guy had stinky ankles.

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:39.719
His feet were like flowers, but
his ankles were, like, rotting.

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:41.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
He had rotten ankles.
-Yeah.

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You've got
to the take care of that,

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:43.856 line:92%
and you've got to know that.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:47.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When you first started
doing "Deal or No Deal" --

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
2005 I guess it was, yes?
-Yes.

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:51.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You had some hesitation,
because, obviously,

00:03:51.431 --> 00:03:52.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
you've been a comedian
for a long time,

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:54.400
and you thought it might affect
your comedy cred,

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.369 size:84% position:42%
which, I would imagine,
I think all comedians

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:57.170 line:92%
have those moments where they --

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:59.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, in 2005,
if you think back,

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:02.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
no comedian had been hosting
a game show

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:06.746
since Groucho Marx or, you know,
maybe Johnny Carson --

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:07.313 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
for decades.

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:10.650
And when your currency is irony
and you're dealing in comedy,

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:14.287
I think the host of a game show
was the punch line.

00:04:14.287 --> 00:04:16.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
So when I got -- And I wasn't
doing good at that time.

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:20.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
In 2005, I wasn't being
booked in a lot of places.

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:20.960 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I wasn't that out there.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:23.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
My career was waning.
I was thinking of quitting.

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:26.099 size:84% position:42%
And then I get the call
from NBC at the time,

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:27.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Can you come do
'Deal or No Deal'?"

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:28.534 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and I said no.

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:29.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then they explained
the game to me,

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:32.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I said,
"Even more reason, no."

00:04:32.372 --> 00:04:35.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's no game, right?
There's no skill.

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:36.876 line:92%
We're just gonna open cases.

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:38.177 line:92%
What am I gonna do for an hour?

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:40.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, I went home,
and I told my wife.

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:41.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
She goes,
"Are you gonna do it?"

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:43.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I said no,
and she goes, "Why?"

00:04:43.283 --> 00:04:45.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "because it'll put
the nail in the coffin

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:47.420 line:92%
of what's left of my career."

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she said, "Where are you
standing right now?"

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:51.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said,
"We're in the kitchen."

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:54.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she said,
"Howie, this is your career."

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:55.295 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.295 --> 00:04:57.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
She said, "You're an idiot.
Take the deal."

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:00.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I did,
and I was so embarrassed.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.334 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I did the show.

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:04.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I had plans
to be funny and witty.

00:05:04.537 --> 00:05:06.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
But when I got onstage and --
this is serious --

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:08.041 line:92%
and I saw the first contestant,

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:09.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they told me
they'd never owned a home,

00:05:09.709 --> 00:05:11.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
they don't have insurance,
it became --

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:14.447
I didn't want to kind of
distract them with being funny.

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:16.649
-Of course.
-I became empathetic, you know?

00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:18.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Even changed my cadence.

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:20.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's why I wanted
to say to somebody,

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:21.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
who wasn't on television,
I would go,

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:26.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
"The offer is...
fifty...thousand...dollars."

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:28.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the reason --
Just like, "Listen to me.

00:05:28.895 --> 00:05:31.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's real,
and this is a chance."

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:31.998 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So I did nothing.

00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:33.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, I flew off
to the Caribbean

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:35.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
where they didn't have TV --
where I didn't have

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:37.236
American television,
'cause I didn't want to see it,

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:39.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I thought
it was gonna be a disaster.

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:42.442
And lo and behold, I got a call,
and they said, "This is a hit."

00:05:42.442 --> 00:05:43.409 line:92%
And I go, "What is a hit?"

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:44.410 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then it aired
the next night,

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:45.778
and they said it was bigger,
and the next night, it's bigger.

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:49.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it became a phenomenon,
and then I flew back to Miami,

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:50.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I landed,
and within seconds,

00:05:50.817 --> 00:05:54.420
the first person came up to me
and went, "Deal or no deal?"

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.121 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And for 10 years,

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:57.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've been clawing
and scraping my way back,

00:05:57.190 --> 00:06:00.893
and the lovely people at CNBC
have given me an opportunity.

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:02.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now,
Wednesday nights on CNBC,

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:06.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
it is bigger and more exciting
than it has ever been.

00:06:06.065 --> 00:06:10.303 size:81% position:41%
It's still $1 million,
26 models, a banker,

00:06:10.303 --> 00:06:13.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
who's now a female banker.
-Good.

00:06:13.506 --> 00:06:14.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is good.
-Yeah.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:17.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-It's about time.

